C R205 OL DEP-012 | DECIDED | Swagger UI through Swashbuckle.AspNetCore is the default interactive API documentation and manual-testing surface in Development (/swagger) rather than a standalone raw OpenAPI endpoint or built-in AddOpenApi()/MapOpenApi(); no second competing documentation stack without a concrete need. | API documentation | none stated
C R206 OL WF-004 | MUST | Verification starts with the final changed-file set and diff: the change matches the requested scope without unrelated refactoring, no generated or build artifacts or secrets were added, temporary diagnostics and probes are removed only after preservation; the final diff is reviewed after all fixes for unrelated edits, commented-out code, temporary logging, TODO/FIXME markers, stale temporary tests or scripts, architecture drift, unapproved drift from the product sources and stale surfaces after a settings change. | verification | none stated
C R207 OL WF-006 | DEFAULT | For a new runnable application or a substantial composition, startup, configuration, persistence or full-stack change verify that the application starts with its Development configuration (API host and endpoint, Swagger UI when expected, configuration binding, database connectivity and initialization, frontend dev server, API base URL and CORS compatibility); a successful build alone does not prove runtime composition. | runtime smoke verification | none stated
C R208 OL RUN-010 | MUST | Before completion remove unused or redundant using directives from every C# file created or modified by the task (including those provided by implicit/global usings unless needed for clarity or disambiguation), verified on the changed files, without an unrelated repository-wide cleanup. | changed C# files | Needed for clarity or disambiguation.
C X25 EX - | MUST | After hook or script changes run the changed script with sample input and confirm both the pass and the failure paths; the maintenance report lists the files changed, owners added or moved and the checker result. | instruction-system maintenance | none stated | Instruction-system maintenance procedure; no oracle policy governs testing or reporting of instruction-system changes. | A hook change applied without exercising its failure path does not follow the procedure.

